\section*{System Overview}
The Cosmos-Encrypted Universe Mapping Engine (CEUME) is a distributed,
fully encrypted cosmology framework that couples:
\begin{itemize}
  \item HEALPix spatial decomposition for sky partitioning,
  \item CKKS fully homomorphic encryption (FHE) noise-budget control,
  \item MPI-based N-body gravitational and MHD plasma solvers,
  \item Telemetry-instrumented verification matrices for physics and crypto.
\end{itemize}

\section*{Core Scientific Contributions}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Encrypted Cosmology Runtime}\\
  End-to-end encrypted ingestion and simulation of DESI, Gaia DR4, and LOFAR
  catalogs without exposing raw coordinates to untrusted nodes.

  \item \textbf{Homomorphic Physics Engine}\\
  N-body gravitational and magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) kernels executed under
  CKKS depth ceilings with dynamic key refresh and bootstrapping control.

  \item \textbf{HEALPix-Aware Domain Decomposition}\\
  Rank assignment via HEALPix tessellation ($N_{\text{side}} = 32$) ensuring
  locality of cross-match and physics operations in equal-area sky tiles.

  \item \textbf{Configuration Curve for FHE Profiles}\\
  Operational modes SECURE\4, BALANCED\8, LAB\12, DEEP\16 defined by
  multiplicative depth budget $L_{\max}$, yield, saturation tolerance, and
  runtime overhead.
\end{enumerate}

